    "Retailers report high foot traffic in city centers like São Paulo, while consumer advocates continue to warn about fake websites and price distrust."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The 2026 Black Friday shopping event in Brazil has demonstrated a significant increase in transactional volume, according to recent market research. While major e-commerce platforms like Mercado Livre and Amazon observed strong demand for electronics and consumer staples, brick-and-mortar stores in urban hubs such as central São Paulo also reported substantial visitor numbers. Despite the growth in sales, the event remains marked by consumer skepticism regarding the authenticity of discounts and reports of fraudulent websites mimicking popular brands. Industry data indicates a shift in payment preferences, with a notable surge in Pix transactions. Although some consumer reports highlight a decline in overall complaints compared to previous years, authorities and watchdogs continue to advise shoppers to remain cautious of phishing attempts and to verify retailer legitimacy before completing purchases during this peak commercial period.",
